{{also|oýnamak}}
==Turkish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|tr|ota|اوینامق|tr=oynamak||to play, perform, risk, disport, move, vibrate, dance, amuse one's self, jest}}, from {{inh|tr|trk-oat||tr=oyna-}}, from {{inh|tr|trk-pro}}. Equivalent to {{m|tr|oyun|gloss=game}} + {{m|tr|-a|gloss=archaic verb forming suffix from nouns}}.
{{rel-top|cognates}}
Cognate with {{cog|xqa||tr=oynāmāk||to play}}, {{cog|otk||tr=oyna-||to play}}, {{cog|az|oynamaq||to play}}, {{cog|ba|уйнау||to play}}, {{cog|kk|ойнау||to play}}, {{cog|kjh|ойнирға||to play}}, {{cog|ky|ойноо||to play}}, {{cog|tk|oýnamak||to play}}, {{cog|ug|ئوينىماق||to play}}, {{cog|uz|oʻynamoq||to play}}, {{cog|sah|оонньоо||to play}}.
{{rel-bottom}}

===Verb===
{{tr-verb|oynar}}

# to [[play]], [[amuse]] oneself, [[fool]] around
# (for a film or play) to be on, be [[playing]]
# to [[dance]]; to [[gambol]], [[cavort]], [[frisk]] about
# to [[move]], [[stir]], [[budge]], [[hop]]
# to [[fluctuate]], [[move]] back and forth, [[flicker]]
# {{lb|tr|transitive}} to [[perform]] (a play), [[play]] (a card)
# to [[risk]], play around with, [[trifle]] with
# to [[monkey]] with, [[tinker]] with, [[tamper]] with

